Commands introduced
kubectl rollout history deployment/NAME - list the numbered revisions the Deployment has rolled out
kubectl rollout history deployment/NAME --revision=N - show the details of one specific revision


ROLLOUT Undo:
Commands introduced
kubectl rollout undo deployment/NAME - roll back to the revision before the current one
kubectl rollout undo deployment/NAME --to-revision=N - roll back to a specific revision number from the history
root@escbash-lab:~# kubectl rollout undo deployment/rollout-web
Warning: resource deployments/rollout-web was previously managed with 'kubectl apply'. Rolling back will not update the kubectl.kubernetes.io/last-applied-configuration annotation, which may cause unexpected behavior on future 'kubectl apply' operations. Consider using 'kubectl apply' with your previous configuration file instead.
deployment.apps/rollout-web rolled back
root@escbash-lab:~# 

SVC Commands introduced
kubectl expose deployment NAME --port=PORT - create a ClusterIP Service in front of a Deployment
kubectl get svc - list the Services in the cluster

